# HARD — 7-step RE visible first; LF handled by background chain

**Scope:** Email processing chat (`EMAIL-PROCESSING-AGENT.md`).

## How it works (EMAIL)

```
AGENT RESPONSE (text-only):
  Phase 1 — Read latest_extract.md (fast tool OK)
  Phase 2 — CHANNEL: EMAIL / Fall # / sections 1-7 as PLAIN chat text
           End with: "Auto-LF filing now."
           STOP. NO fill_case_tracker. NO --closeout-* here.

BACKGROUND (automatic — no agent involvement):
  re_complete_sound_hook detects section 7 -> spawns auto_lf_after_re.py
  auto_lf_after_re.py -> fill_case_tracker.py + --closeout-* + Dexter sound

PATH B SAFETY NET (hook, silent):
  extract_auto_continue_hook Path B detects latest_re_visible.md has
  section 7 but auto_lf_done.json missing -> silently spawns
  auto_lf_after_re.py — NO chat message fires.
```

**Order lock:** 7-step text MUST be visible in chat before LF fires.
**Agent rule:** After writing sections 1-7, STOP. Never call fill_case_tracker or --closeout-*.
Running those tools in the agent response collapses the 7-step into a hidden dropdown — forbidden.

## Why no LF tools in agent response

When a long-running tool (--closeout-anwenden) runs in the same agent turn as the 7-step text,
Cursor groups the entire response into a "Finished background tasks" collapsible dropdown. The
operator loses visibility of the RE. The background chain avoids this entirely.

## Hard bans

1. fill_case_tracker / --closeout-* in the same agent response as the 7-step text
2. Writing the 7-step then running LF tools in a "Response 2" — forbidden
3. Writing "sound hook handles LF" as permission to idle after the 7-step
4. Task/explore subagents for RE or LF
5. [AUTO_PIPELINE_TURN_C] — obsolete, blocked, must not be processed

## Self-check (before writing anything for Fall #N)

- About to call fill_case_tracker before the 7-step text? STOP — write 7-step first.
- 7-step already visible for #N? Background LF may already be running — skip duplicate RE.

## Sounds = operator audio cues only

Prowler / book / Dexter notify the operator when off-screen. They do not run Auto-LF and do
not excuse skipping the 7-step. The background chain (sound hook -> auto_lf_after_re.py)
handles LF silently after section 7 is written.

## CALL exception

CHANNEL: CALL -> Auto-LF voice immediately in same turn (no email 7-step, no dropdown risk).

